instr:
Support Brickadia world round trips in brs-js

I'd like to build Brickadia worlds and prefabs with `brs-js`, read them back from `.brz` archives, and save the same content to revisioned `.brdb` databases. This needs to cover bricks, components, wires, owners, entities, and microchip sub-grids.

For example, building and reopening a microchip prefab should work like this:

```ts
import { World, WorldReader } from 'brs-js';
const world = new World();
const { grid } = world.addMicrochip({ position: [30, 0, 2] });
world.addBrick({ position: [10, 0, 2] }, grid);
world.makePrefab({ isMicrochipPrefab: true });
const reader = WorldReader.from(world.toBrz());
```

The resulting archive should expose the prefab metadata and linked inner grid through the reader. The same builder should also work with `Brdb.save`. Expected behavior is documented in the API doc comments and `README.md`'s “Brickadia Worlds (.brz, .brdb)” section, including “World builder” and “.brdb (SQLite worlds)”.

Currently, `World.addMicrochip` and the other incomplete methods throw “not implemented”. Complete the stubs in `src/brdb/`: `bits.ts`, `brdb.ts`, `brz.ts`, `bytes.ts`, `guid.ts`, `reader.ts`, `schema.ts`, `soaWriters.ts`, `world.ts`, and `writePlan.ts`, plus `src/uuid.ts` and the supporting helper in `test/brdb/fixtures.ts`. These include archive navigation, schema values, binary serialization, UUID conversion, and database revisions.

The package's own tests must keep passing, and existing exported API name
